flowchart TB
%% IMPLEMENT AND TEST PIPELINE. Split from pipeline.mmd.
%% Input: the plan file from the planning pipeline.
%% Starts at "implement task".
%% Ends by locking the source repo and handing a finished implementation to the
%% rebase and merge pipeline, or with an exit.
%% Rules that apply everywhere, not steps:
%%   1. Every git interaction goes through a script. Never prose.
%%   2. Every read and write of tasks.json is atomic.
%%   3. Never update a test that was not created in this task's worktree,
%%      unless that test is broken or asserts nothing.
%%   4. "fix the codebase" edits source, not tests.
%%   5. Never progress past a suite run until every test passes.
%%   6. Every test loop runs commit the work -> test the work -> repair the work.
%%      A repair is never tested until it is committed, so each loop re-enters at
%%      its "commit if needed" box, never at the test box.
%%   7. "commit if needed" commits nothing when the worktree is clean. Its message
%%      is derived, not chosen: the run's first commit is the work, and every
%%      commit after it is a repair to code that made tests fail.
%%   8. Every box that touches the working tree operates on every repository
%%      layer, deepest submodule first, root last: commit and run tests both walk
%%      the same occurrence tree. Boxes that only read or write tasks.json do not.
%%   9. A script that fails operationally, as opposed to returning a verdict,
%%      exits the run as run-failed. No step is retried after it has mutated
%%      anything. The task is already active and a worktree already exists here,
%%      so the exit workflow always runs in full.
%%  10. "lock the source repo" holds one lock on the source repository for the
%%      whole tail of the run, across the rebase and merge pipeline and the exit
%%      workflow. The lock is a durable file, acquired and released by different
%%      processes, owned by "runId:taskNumber" - NOT by runId alone, because
%%      every task workflow in one invocation shares a runId and would otherwise
%%      read a sibling's lock as its own. Exactly one box releases it: "clean up"
%%      on success, "release the worktree lease and the source lock if held" on
%%      every exit. Both live in the exit workflow.
%%  11. A mutating box whose result is lost is never blindly retried and never
%%      assumed failed. Each one, including a test box that records its result,
%%      has a read-only reconciliation check that reads the world and decides
%%      whether it already happened. A safe idempotent rerun happens only after
%%      reconciliation proves it did not complete. Only an ambiguous loss is
%%      run-failed.
%% Diamond definitions where the name alone is not enough:
%%   do the task tests pass?           - the test run alone decides this; codex
%%                                       judges the tests, the tests judge the work
%% Exit types this pipeline can produce:
%%   tests-red          - task tests still failing after 2 fix attempts
%%   tests-flagged      - codex flagged the tests twice
%%   run-failed         - a script failed operationally
%% run-failed is deliberately not drawn as an edge. It can leave ANY green box,
%% so drawing it would add one edge per box and hide the flow. Rule 9 is its
%% specification: a non-zero exit from any script goes straight to the exit
%% workflow with exit type run-failed and the script's stderr as the note.
%% The committed, green implementation this pipeline emits is the input to the
%% rebase and merge pipeline.

  A["implement task"] --> NOTES["record implementation notes file to tasks.json"]
  NOTES --> CW["commit if needed"]
  CW --> TT["run task tests"]
  TT --> QTF{"do the tests fail?"}
  QTF -- "yes, under 2 attempts" --> FIXT["fix the codebase"]
  FIXT --> CW
  QTF -- "yes, after 2 attempts<br/>exit type: tests-red<br/>exit note: task tests failed after 2 codebase fixes" --> EXITWF
  QTF -- no --> RT["codex reviews tests against task details and plan file"]
  RT --> QCX{"are the tests flagged?"}
  QCX -- "yes, under 2 attempts" --> AMT["amend the tests"]
  AMT --> CW
  QCX -- "yes, after 2 attempts<br/>exit type: tests-flagged<br/>exit note: codex flagged the tests twice" --> EXITWF
  QCX -- no --> RB["lock the source repo"]
  RB --> IMPL["finished implementation"]

  EXITWF["exit workflow"]

  classDef script fill:#2f7d46,stroke:#1e5c31,color:#ffffff
  classDef prose fill:#e0b400,stroke:#a88600,color:#1a1a1a
  classDef output fill:#3b6ea5,stroke:#254a70,color:#ffffff
  class NOTES,CW,TT,QTF,QCX,RB script
  class A,RT,FIXT,AMT prose
  class IMPL,EXITWF output
